<Shell title="About Langston" section="about"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PLAYBOOK</p><h1>Hi, I’m Langston.</h1><p class="lede">I’m learning, building, and finding ways to make technology easier to understand.</p></header><div class="about-layout"><div class="about-story"><p>I’m an IT Support Intern at Wolters Kluwer and a graduate student studying artificial intelligence at Kennesaw State University. I earned my B.S. in Computer Information Systems with a minor in Cybersecurity at WCU, class of 2026.</p><p>I also ran track in college. That experience is part of who I am, alongside my interest in technology and the work I’m doing now.</p><h2>A clearer place to begin</h2><p>I created this playbook to help people who are new to using AI improve their websites and apps. You shouldn’t have to know all the right design terms before you can ask a useful question.</p><p>My goal is simple: help you understand what a prompt does, make it your own, and feel more confident taking the next step. I’m still learning too, and I want this to be a welcoming place to start.</p><a class="button primary" href="/start">Try your first prompt</a></div><section class="panel about-facts"><p class="tiny">A LITTLE ABOUT ME</p><dl><dt>Work</dt><dd>IT Support Intern<br/>Wolters Kluwer</dd><dt>Graduate studies</dt><dd>M.S. in Artificial Intelligence<br/>Kennesaw State University</dd><dt>Education</dt><dd>B.S. in Computer Information Systems<br/>Cybersecurity minor · WCU ’26</dd><dt>Beyond the screen</dt><dd>Former college track athlete</dd></dl><p class="quiet">This is my personal project, independent of my employer and universities.</p></section></div></Shell>
